A||N||3||Kage86GT4SP||Pilot bearing/bushing?||||1||
Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||03-10-2001||03:05 PM||||My brother is in the middle of a 4spd/5spd swap.  He's got the old out, and putting the new in, he discovers what he's calling a "mighty big hole in the crank face" which has him understandibly paranoid about the need for a pilot bushing.  Is there one?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>86 SE 2.8 4 spd (5spd in the garage, and turbo on the shelf) <P>87 Camaro TT w/89 383 vette stroker,TPI,700R4,MSD6A,Blaster,Accel,SLP Stainless Headers,Edelbrock Cat Back. <P>72 Pinto Wgn <BR>85 5.0L H.O., B&M, AOD, MSD, Accel, Sony, lowered, shaved, tinted, WHITE<p>[This message has been edited by Kage86GT4SP (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||03-10-2001||06:15 PM||||Don't worry, be happy!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you look at the input shaft of any Fiero manual transaxle, you will see that it does not stick out far enough (if at all) to even fit into the crank!<P>There is no need for a pilot bushing in the crank, never was one from the factory (manual transaxles only ...)<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||10
Z||000002||Kage86GT4SP||03-11-2001||06:13 AM||||Thank you sir, and I'll pass it along!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric_PA||03-11-2001||07:29 AM||||I am very glad to see this post and here that there is no need for a bushing. It was my biggest worry since I put my 84 back together. I didn't find any in it when I took it appart, but my dad was around when I put in the new clutch and he insisted that there should be one, but I told him that there wasn't one when I took it appart and the autoparts store didn't have one listed.<BR>Eric||||reg||7
